      "content": "Libertarians ground their absolute property rights in the Lockean labor theory, arguing that individuals own themselves and their labor, so any appropriation of that labor without consent is theft. They further contend that the state's monopoly on force is illegitimate because it violates the natural right to self-ownership, making taxation a form of forced labor that destroys the very freedom it claims to protect. Their logic is that without these strict boundaries, the state inevitably becomes a tyrant that erodes all other liberties, so protecting property is the only way to preserve true individual autonomy.",
